        <body>
            <div xml:id="d768">

                <pb facs="0709" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1937v03/pg702"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.01/556</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Memorandum by the Chief of the Division of Far Eastern
                        Affairs</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >of a Conversation With the Second Secretary of the Chinese Embassy</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Tsui</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1937-11-20">November 20, 1937</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Tsui called at the Department and presented the attached copy of the “Text of
                    a statement issued by the Chinese Government on November 20, 1937, in regard to
                    the removal of the national capital from Nanking to Chungking”.</p>
                <p>Mr. Tsui said that in presenting by hand the copy of the aforementioned statement
                    he wished to inform the Department that although the Chinese Government is
                    moving in its entirety to Chungking, the Foreign Office, and possibly other
                    governmental agencies, will, at least for the time being, maintain branch
                    offices at Hankow, as in the past branch offices have been maintained at
                    Shanghai.</p>
                <p>Mr. Mackay thanked Mr. Tsui for bringing this matter to the attention of the
                    Department.</p>
                <closer><signed>M[<hi rendition="#small-caps">axwell</hi>] M. H[<hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">amilton</hi>]</signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d768-a1.xml" xpointer="d768-a1"/>
